  dropped appear as the single opaque token EXTRA.
  [PASS] S3 THE PREDICTOR IS EXACT.  G(sigma_raw(h)) reproduces menu(h) ENTRYWISE with exact Fraction weights on every history of the family (depth 6) — same event set, same weights, no history data consulted.  G is a FUNCTION OF sigma's raw tuple by construction, so this is (H1) reduced to G's own correctness rather than to a sweep  (histories = 34375; mismatches = 0)
  [PASS] S3(b) THE DROPPED BASE IS UNAMBIGUOUS.  At most ONE base is mentioned by the menu but dropped by sigma, and it is always the cone-alive base X[a] of the unique actor with hold[a] = None (and no live proposal).  So the single EXTRA token is forced: renaming it costs no information and the renamed menus of sigma-equal histories coincide  (dropped-base count spectrum = {0: 29547, 1: 4828}; ambiguous cases = 0)
  [PASS] S3(d) THE CLOSED FORM'S COROLLARIES, all forced by G and all exact: every idle weight is 3/4; every propose weight is 1/8; every SELF-arb weight is 1/4; every PAIR-arb ("blind") weight is 1/8 and they come in twos — so EVERY BLIND GROUP SUMS TO EXACTLY 1/4.  Hence the per-actor menu mass is 1 or 5/4 and the total is 2 or 5/2 — NOT 9/4: a per-actor 5/4 needs a TWO-member full-view component, which by (5b) carries BOTH actors' proposals, so the actors reach 5/4 together or not at all (round-1 MINOR 4).  This DERIVES d42b3's G-L2 quarter-quantization, which that receipt could only gate and scope  (propose weights = ['1/8']; self-arb = ['1/4']; pair-arb = ['1/8']; per-actor masses = ['1', '5/4']; totals = ['2', '5/2'])
